  putreg32((uint32_t)(mtimecmp >> 32), CTIMER_MTIMECMPH);

  set_csr(mie, MIP_MTIP);

  /* Process the OS tick */
  nxsched_process_timer();
}
```

Also add a one-time marker: static int g_tick_count = 0; if (g_tick_count < 3) { riscv_lowputc('!'); g_tick_count++; }

## Fix 3: GPLL lock bit — check correct register/bit

In rv1126b_clockconfig.c, the SDK confirms GPLL lock is at GPLL_CON[2] bit 10 (TOPCRU + 0x28 bit 10), NOT GPLL_CON[0] bit 31.

Change:
```c
#define GPLL_CON0_ADDR        (TOPCRU_BASE + 0x0020)
#define GPLL_CON0_LOCK_SHIFT  31
#define GPLL_CON0_LOCK_MASK   (1 << GPLL_CON0_LOCK_SHIFT)
```
To:
```c
/* SDK-verified: GPLL lock status is at GPLL_CON[2] bit 10 */
#define GPLL_LOCK_ADDR        (TOPCRU_BASE + 0x0028)
#define GPLL_LOCK_SHIFT       10
#define GPLL_LOCK_MASK        (1 << GPLL_LOCK_SHIFT)
```

And update `rv1126b_wait_pll_lock()` and `rv1126b_ensure_gpll_locked()` to use the new names.

## Fix 4: Post-G diagnostic markers

Add markers in these functions (just riscv_lowputc calls):

In rv1126b_timerisr.c `up_timer_initialize()`: print 'T' at entry, 't' at end.
In rv1126b_serial.c `riscv_serialinit()`: print 'S' at entry, 's' after /dev/console, '0' after /dev/ttyS0.
In rv1126b_allocateheap.c `riscv_addregion()`: print 'H'.

## Build and package

After all edits:
1. cd /home/lijian/project/open-vela && export PATH=/home/lijian/project/open-vela/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86_64/riscv-none-elf/bin:$PATH && ./build.sh vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_135_board/configs/nsh -j8
2. riscv-none-elf-objcopy -O binary nuttx nuttx.bin
3. cp nuttx.bin to SDK Image/rtt.bin
4. mkimage -f amp.its -E -p 0xe00 nuttx_amp.img (use absolute path to mkimage tool if needed)
5. Replace output/firmware/amp.img
6. ./build.sh updateimg

Report all changes, build status, and expected marker sequence.

